Here is a program that reads the C# code and provides assert statement based on the comments with "@@@" prefix.

```Csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Runtime.InteropServices;

namespace ConsoleApplication1
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string filePath =  @"C:\Users\username\Documents\file.cs";
            string line;
            StreamReader file = new StreamReader(filePath);
            while ((line = file.ReadLine()) != null)
            {
                // Replace new line character to end of line. 
                line = line.Replace("\r\n", " ");
                if (line.Contains("@@@"))
                {
                    string[] words = line.Split(' ');
                    foreach (string word in words)
                        if (word.StartsWith("@@@"))
                        {
                            string comment = word.Substring(3).Trim();
                            Console.WriteLine("Debug.Assert(" + comment + ");");
                        }
                }
            }
            file.Close();
        }
    }
}
```

This program reads the file line by line and checks each line for the occurrence of "@@@". When it finds a line with "@@@", it gets the comment part, splits it into words and for each word, if it has a "@@@" prefix, it removes the prefix and prints the word as an assertion statement. 

